#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:1
msgid "aws4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:4
msgid ""
"A small utility to sign [vanilla Node.js "
"http(s)](https://nodejs.org/api/http.html) request options using Amazon's"
" [AWS Signature Version 4](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr"
"/signature-version-4.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:7
msgid ""
"If you want to sign and send AWS requests using "
"[`fetch()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Fetch_API), "
"then check out [aws4fetch](https://github.com/mhart/aws4fetch) – "
"otherwise you can also bundle this library for use [in older "
"browsers](./browser)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:9
msgid ""
"The only AWS service I know of that *doesn't* support v4 is "
"[SimpleDB](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonSimpleDB/latest/DeveloperGuide/SDB_API.html)"
" (it only supports [AWS Signature Version "
"2](https://github.com/mhart/aws2))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:13
msgid ""
"It also provides defaults for a number of core AWS headers and request "
"parameters, making it very easy to query AWS services, or build out a "
"fully-featured AWS library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:17
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:135
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:138
msgid "aws4.sign(requestOptions, [credentials])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:140
msgid ""
"Calculates and populates any necessary AWS headers and/or request options"
" on `requestOptions`. Returns `requestOptions` as a convenience for "
"chaining."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:143
msgid ""
"`requestOptions` is an object holding the same options that the Node.js "
"[http.request](https://nodejs.org/docs/latest/api/http.html#http_http_request_options_callback)"
" function takes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:147
msgid ""
"The following properties of `requestOptions` are used in the signing or "
"populated if they don't already exist:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:150
msgid ""
"`hostname` or `host` (will try to be determined from `service` and "
"`region` if not given)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:151
msgid "`method` (will use `'GET'` if not given or `'POST'` if there is a `body`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:152
msgid "`path` (will use `'/'` if not given)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:153
msgid "`body` (will use `''` if not given)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:154
msgid ""
"`service` (will try to be calculated from `hostname` or `host` if not "
"given)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:155
msgid ""
"`region` (will try to be calculated from `hostname` or `host` or use "
"`'us-east-1'` if not given)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:156
msgid ""
"`signQuery` (to sign the query instead of adding an `Authorization` "
"header, defaults to false)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:157
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`extraHeadersToIgnore` (an object with lowercase header keys to ignore "
"when signing, eg `{ 'content-length': true }`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:158
msgid ""
"`extraHeadersToInclude` (an object with lowercase header keys to include "
"when signing, overriding any ignores)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:159
msgid ""
"`headers['Host']` (will use `hostname` or `host` or be calculated if not "
"given)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:160
msgid ""
"`headers['Content-Type']` (will use `'application/x-www-form-urlencoded; "
"charset=utf-8'` if not given and there is a `body`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/aws4_README.md:162
msgid ""
"`headers['Date']` (used to calculate the signature date if given, "
"otherwise `new Date` is used)"
msgstr ""

